00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:03.620
for that unit proceeds.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:09.260
The case on both sides, in Rio, is when a school should expel a student after a serious

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:09.620
assault.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:16.020
Ten days ago, at Unit 2 of Collegio Iconé, Intacuara, a physical education teacher referring

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.620
a football match marked a foul.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.120
Some students disagreed and attacked him.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.200
Police were called.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.340
The school suspended those involved.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.920
A general counsel of the network then decided they should not remain.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:32.620
For Nando Venoncio, the school's maintainer and director general says three students had their

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:38.660
enrollment locked, which he describes as expulsion. He says that step sits on a scale already explained

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:45.660
at matriculation. Verbal warnings, written warnings, suspensions, then closure of enrollment. He says

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:50.820
the school suspended them at once, supported the teacher, reviewed the images, called a council,

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:55.560
and brought in the families because they have a right to speak. The teacher is a way in receiving

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:00.460
the school's support. The adolescents were summoned to testify at the 32nd police station

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.760
in Tacuara, and the Guardian Ship Council is following the case.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:09.360
Vinanzio says the school will still, this year, review protocols for interclass games,

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.140
hold a talk on competitiveness, and meet a representative of the Jacquerapagua area

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:19.000
Guardian Ship Council on school safety, relationships, and the consequences of acts.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:24.780
Monica Doneto-Getas, a psychoanalyst in parent guide, argues that violence is a limit

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:29.120
that cannot be crossed or treated as normal, because force breaks the use of words.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.580
She separates a fight between students, which she says the school should mediate,

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:37.960
from an attack on a teacher, which she calls an attack on authority and on the rule.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:42.960
She argues that expulsion also tells the other students that aggression is not an accepted

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.500
way to end a conflict, and that families have to help build limits.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:51.200
Priscilla Montez, a specialist in neuroeducation and child development,

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.600
argues that the useful question is which step protects the school community and

00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:00.560
still teaches in proportion. Not which punishment the student deserves. She says

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.940
a bad act is not an identity and that a purely punitive answer can push a

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:08.860
student further from school. She argues that a transfer does not end the

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:12.880
schools and the family's responsibility. That schooling should continue and

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:16.560
that moving a student with nerve plan for the behavior can carry the problem

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:23.440
somewhere else. Natalia Zavir, a pedagogue at Afia Unigran Rio, argues that expulsion can be used

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.700
when other strategies are not enough or when there is a concrete risk to the community,

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:33.620
and that a right to education is not tolerance of violence. She says the gravity has to be proved.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:39.640
Her list includes serious physical assault, persistent threats, repeated bullying or cyberbullying,

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:45.760
harassment, discrimination, caring weapons, drug trafficking, and intentional destruction that

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:46.740
puts people at risk.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.700
Every day in discipline, low achievement, one-off conflicts,

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.560
undone assignments, or family disagreements

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:56.300
with the school, do not justify expulsion, she says.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:59.400
And a student should not be punished for acts done only

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:00.960
by the adults responsible for them.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:04.460
Gabriel DeBrito Silva, a lawyer, argues

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.400
that expulsion must stay reasonable relative to the act,

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.620
repeated disciplinary offenses, insubordination,

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:13.520
disrespective staff, and a serious insult

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:18.480
can allow enrollment to be closed or not renewed, he says, only if the rights to a full defense

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:22.700
and to answer the case are respected, under a procedure based on an ethics code

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:27.940
or the school's internal rules. The speakers accept that students physically attack the teacher

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:33.520
and that the school has to protect its community. Inside the school, the noncios next steps are

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:37.980
that protocol review, the competitiveness talk, and the guardianship council meeting,

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:42.740
all still this year, while the police station and the guardianship council follow the case.

